Feature: Points and the end of the game
  Each tower that a team holds gives the team one point each second. The first team to 500
  points wins. If no team has 500 points when the clock gets to 0, the team with more points
  wins. Equal points at the end is a draw. When the game stops, the scores and the towers do
  not change.

  Expectation: Each tower that a team holds gives one point each second
    Given the towers held by Blue are 2
    And the score of Blue is 0 points
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the score of Blue is 20 points

  Expectation: The first team to 500 points wins
    Given the towers held by Blue are at least 1
    And the score of Blue is 495 points
    And the score of Red is at most 400 points
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the game of Towers is won by Blue
    And the score of Blue is 500 points

  Expectation: When the clock gets to 0, the team with more points wins
    Given the time left is 5 s
    And the score of Blue is 200 points
    And the score of Red is 300 points
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the game of Towers is won by Red
    And the time left is 0 s

  Expectation: Equal points when the clock gets to 0 is a draw
    Given the time left is 5 s
    And the score of Blue is 300 points
    And the score of Red is 300 points
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the game of Towers is a draw

  Expectation: A game that has stopped does not change
    The scores stay as they were at the end, and so do the towers. Nobody can take a tower
    after the game stops.

    Given the game of Towers is won by Blue
    When the game runs for 1 minute
    Then the score of Blue stays the same
